          "reason": "For every tagged scalable compound $c$, the mass in [[def-tdmath-tagged-scalable-compound]] is independent of the finite summation set used. Boundary endpoints: No interval endpoint remains implicit in the Statement.",
          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Statement",
            "source_excerpt": "For every tagged scalable compound $c$, the mass in [[def-tdmath-tagged-scalable-compound]] is independent of the finite summation set used. For any compounds $c,d$ and $t\\ge0$, $m(c+d)=m(c)+m(d)$ and $m(tc)=t m(c)$; $m(0)=0$. For every $x\\in X$, the unit-state compound $e_x$ has $m(e_x)=1$. A compound has zero mass if and only if it is the empty compound.",
            "current_raw_sha256": "4e2313ceb48b58d07a755229f743ed487a94e870ed47423da5f9a9f7318170c4",
            "scope_only_not_proof_acceptance": true
