          "reason": "Assume the strict-reference hypotheses and let $S$ be the normalized representation from [[thm-tdmath-additive-entropy-representation]]. Boundary nonempty-choice: No arbitrary choice is used; any existence argument is for the fixed finite or individual case.",
          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Statement",
            "source_excerpt": "Assume the strict-reference hypotheses and let $S$ be the normalized representation from [[thm-tdmath-additive-entropy-representation]]. Let $T:X\\to\\mathbb R$ be another additive extensive representation of the same comparisons: for every finite compound $C=\\sum_i c_i e_{x_i}$ define $T(C):=\\sum_i c_iT(x_i)$, and require $C\\preceq D$ iff $T(C)\\le T(D)$ whenever $m(C)=m(D)$. Then there are unique $a>0$ and $b\\in\\mathbb R$ such that $T(x)=aS(x)+b$ for every $x\\in X$. Conversely every such positive affine change represents the same comparisons.",
