          "source": "lem-tdmath-reference-supremum-bounds",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume [[def-tdmath-comparison-and-stability]] on compounds over a nonempty state set $X$, a strict reference pair $x_0\\preceq x_1$ with not $x_1\\preceq x_0$, and the complete ordered field $\\mathbb R$. For $x\\in X$ define\n\n$$L_x:=\\{\\lambda\\in\\mathbb R:R_\\lambda\\preceq_s e_x\\}.$$\n\nThen $L_x$ is nonempty, bounded above, and downward closed. Its supremum $S(x):=\\sup L_x$ is a real number and satisfies $R_{S(x)}\\sim_s e_x$. Stability is used to prove attainment; no continuity of states or order is assumed.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
