        {
          "case": "endpoints",
          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "Let $\\mathcal G$ be a set of formal type labels closed under the formal operations $(\\Gamma,\\Gamma')\\mapsto\\Gamma\\times\\Gamma'$ and $(t,\\Gamma)\\mapsto t\\Gamma$ for every real $t>0$. Boundary endpoints: No interval endpoint remains implicit in the Statement.",
          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Definition",
            "source_excerpt": "Let $\\mathcal G$ be a set of formal type labels closed under the formal operations $(\\Gamma,\\Gamma')\\mapsto\\Gamma\\times\\Gamma'$ and $(t,\\Gamma)\\mapsto t\\Gamma$ for every real $t>0$. Let $F:=\\mathbb R^{(\\mathcal G)}$ be the vector space of finite-support real functions on $\\mathcal G$, and let $e_\\Gamma$ be the function equal to $1$ at $\\Gamma$ and $0$ elsewhere.\n\nForm the set of relation vectors\n\n$$\\mathcal R:=\\{e_{\\Gamma\\times\\Gamma'}-e_\\Gamma-e_{\\Gamma'}:\\Gamma,\\Gamma'\\in\\mathcal G\\}\\cup\\{e_{t\\Gamma}-t e_\\Gamma:t>0,\\Gamma\\in\\mathcal G\\}.$$\n\nLet $N$ be the set of all finite real linear combinations of members of $\\mathcal R$, and define the **type-offset vector space**\n\n$$V_{\\mathcal G}:=F/N.$$\n\nThe class of $c\\in F$ is $[c]$. The defining relations are $[e_{\\Gamma\\times\\Gamma'}]=[e_\\Gamma]+[e_{\\Gamma'}]$ and $[e_{t\\Gamma}]=t[e_\\Gamma]$. The set existence, subspace properties, quotient operations and vector-space laws are proved in [[lem-tdmath-type-offset-vector-space-well-defined]]. These are formal algebraic type labels; no actual catalyst-chain cost or physical existence claim is built into $V_{\\mathcal G}$.",
            "current_raw_sha256": "deb4d35d92d9170aea9901d49baa8f5cbc3c0be48133ac18c614944391e85404",
            "scope_only_not_proof_acceptance": true
          }
