          "reason": "For the construction in [[def-tdmath-type-offset-vector-space]], $F$ and $N$ are sets, $F$ is a real vector space, $N$ is a linear subspace of $F$, and $F/N$ has representative-independent vector operations making it a real vector space. Boundary one: No one-element boundary changes the result beyond the stated hypotheses.",
          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Statement",
            "source_excerpt": "For the construction in [[def-tdmath-type-offset-vector-space]], $F$ and $N$ are sets, $F$ is a real vector space, $N$ is a linear subspace of $F$, and $F/N$ has representative-independent vector operations making it a real vector space. Its displayed product and positive-scaling relations hold in the quotient.",
            "current_raw_sha256": "8f7f6b0115ea147cbe259ad483ddff3c0ca52ecbb5641d3ab6c23c97554a8080",
