            "source_excerpt": "Take two types with fixed totals $T_1=T_2=1$ and a common meter satisfying the compatibility hypotheses of [[thm-tdmath-common-meter-calibration]]. Let type-1 states $a_0,a_1$ have normalized values $0,1$, and type-2 states $b_0,b_1$ have normalized values $1/3,3$. Using the shared raw state tags of that theorem, let $C_0=e_{a_{1,a_1}}+e_{a_{2,b_0}}$ and $D_0=e_{a_{1,a_0}}+e_{a_{2,b_1}}$. Their fixed-meter encodings are $C=C_0+2e_{z_0}$ and $D=D_0+2e_{z_0}$, each of mass four. The calibrated values are $4/3$ for $C$ and $3$ for $D$; the common-meter comparison orders $C\\preceq D$ and, after common-meter cancellation, $C_0\\preceq D_0$.",
            "current_raw_sha256": "6b13ea6c698ea682cee51d31840ce521c73f26bd236f9559a9bd29312386ac18",
